Table full name: USDA_NASS_AGRICULTURE.USDA_NASS_AGRICULTURE.ENVIRONMENTAL
Column name: sector_desc Type: TEXT Description: Five high level, broad categories useful to narrow down choices (CROPS, ANIMALS & PRODUCTS, ECONOMICS, DEMOGRAPHICS, and ENVIRONMENTAL).
Column name: domaincat_desc Type: TEXT Description: Categories or partitions within a domain (e.g., under domain = SALES, domain categories include $1,000 TO $9,999, $10,000 TO $19,999, etc).
Column name: state_name Type: TEXT Description: State full name.
Column name: commodity_desc Type: TEXT Description: The primary subject of interest (e.g., CORN, CATTLE, LABOR, TRACTORS, OPERATORS).
Column name: prodn_practice_desc Type: TEXT Description: A method of production or action taken on the commodity (e.g., IRRIGATED, ORGANIC, ON FEED).
Column name: state_fips_code Type: NUMBER Description: NASS 2-digit state codes; include 99 and 98 for US TOTAL and OTHER STATES, respectively; otherwise match ANSI codes.
Column name: watershed_code Type: NUMBER Description: US Geological Survey (USGS) 8-digit Hydrologic Unit Code (HUC) for watersheds.
Column name: load_time Type: NUMBER Description: Date and time indicating when record was inserted into Quick Stats database.
Column name: source_desc Type: TEXT Description: Source of data (CENSUS or SURVEY). Census program includes the Census of Ag as well as follow up projects. Survey program includes national, state, and county surveys.
Column name: county_name Type: TEXT Description: County name.
Column name: util_practice_desc Type: TEXT Description: Utilizations (e.g., GRAIN, FROZEN, SLAUGHTER) or marketing channels (e.g., FRESH MARKET, PROCESSING, RETAIL).
Column name: county_ansi Type: NUMBER Description: ANSI standard 3-digit county codes.
Column name: begin_code Type: NUMBER Description: If applicable, a 2-digit code corresponding to the beginning of the reference period (e.g., for freq_desc = MONTHLY, begin_code ranges from 01 (January) to 12 (December)).
Column name: zip_5 Type: NUMBER Description: US Postal Service 5-digit zip code.
Column name: watershed_desc Type: TEXT Description: Name assigned to the HUC.
Column name: week_ending Type: DATE Description: Week ending date, used when freq_desc = WEEKLY.
Column name: region_desc Type: TEXT Description: NASS defined geographic entities not readily defined by other standard geographic levels. A region can be a less than a state (SUB-STATE) or a group of states (MULTI-STATE), and may be specific to a commodity.
Column name: county_code Type: NUMBER Description: NASS 3-digit county codes; includes 998 for OTHER (COMBINED) COUNTIES and Alaska county codes; otherwise match ANSI codes.
Column name: short_desc Type: TEXT Description: A concatenation of six columns: commodity_desc, class_desc, prodn_practice_desc, util_practice_desc, statisticcat_desc, and unit_desc.
Column name: asd_code Type: NUMBER Description: NASS defined county groups, unique within a state, 2-digit ag statistics district code.
Column name: reference_period_desc Type: TEXT Description: The specific time frame, within a freq_desc.
Column name: class_desc Type: TEXT Description: Generally a physical attribute (e.g., variety, size, color, gender) of the commodity.
Column name: domain_desc Type: TEXT Description: Generally another characteristic of operations that produce a particular commodity (e.g., ECONOMIC CLASS, AREA OPERATED, NAICS CLASSIFICATION, SALES). For chemical usage data, the domain describes the type of chemical applied to the commodity. The domain = TOTAL will have no further breakouts; i.e., the data value pertains completely to the short_desc.
Column name: unit_desc Type: TEXT Description: The unit associated with the statistic category (e.g., ACRES, $ / LB, HEAD, $, OPERATIONS).
Column name: asd_desc Type: TEXT Description: Ag statistics district name.
Column name: statisticcat_desc Type: TEXT Description: The aspect of a commodity being measured (e.g., AREA HARVESTED, PRICE RECEIVED, INVENTORY, SALES).
Column name: country_code Type: NUMBER Description: US Census Bureau, Foreign Trade Division 4-digit country code, as of April, 2007.
Column name: country_name Type: TEXT Description: Country name.
Column name: agg_level_desc Type: TEXT Description: Aggregation level or geographic granularity of the data (e.g., STATE, AG DISTRICT, COUNTY, REGION, ZIP CODE).
Column name: group_desc Type: TEXT Description: Subsets within sector (e.g., under sector = CROPS, the groups are FIELD CROPS, FRUIT & TREE NUTS, HORTICULTURE, and VEGETABLES).
Column name: cv_percent Type: FLOAT Description: Coefficient of variation. Available for the 2012 Census of Agriculture only. County-level CVs are generalized.
Column name: location_desc Type: TEXT Description: Full description for the location dimension.
Column name: congr_district_code Type: NUMBER Description: US Congressional District 2-digit code.
Column name: value Type: FLOAT Description: Published data value.
Column name: year Type: NUMBER Description: The numeric year of the data.
Column name: value_suppression_code Type: TEXT Description: Any suppression codes used to avoid displaying data that should not be disclosed or from putting out data lower than the precision level defined by NASS. Code definitions can be found in the NASS publications.
Column name: state_ansi Type: NUMBER Description: American National Standards Institute (ANSI) standard 2-digit state codes.
Column name: cv_suppression_code Type: TEXT Description: Any suppression codes used to avoid displaying data that should not be disclosed or from putting out data lower than the precision level defined by NASS. Code definitions can be found in the NASS publications.
Column name: end_code Type: NUMBER Description: If applicable, a 2-digit code corresponding to the end of the reference period (e.g., the reference period of JAN THRU MAR will have begin_code = 01 and end_code = 03).
Column name: state_alpha Type: TEXT Description: State abbreviation, 2-character alpha code.
Column name: freq_desc Type: TEXT Description: Length of time covered (ANNUAL, SEASON, MONTHLY, WEEKLY, POINT IN TIME). MONTHLY often covers more than one month. POINT IN TIME is as of a particular day.
Sample rows:
